extends RefCounted
const TEXT = """[b][color=#d5b87a]v0.4 · Read the fight, test the dice[/color][/b]

[b]A larger chronicle on the right.[/b] The entire event stream stays visible in a tall, scrollable panel. Each entry separates round, event type and result. Full history, filters and copying remain available because three lines hid important outcomes.

[b]A clear active turn.[/b] A large colored banner names the acting hero or boss. The active party card has a colored border, and an arrow marked TURN follows the active hero on the board. This makes shared rolls easier to distinguish from individual turns.

[b]Smoother presentation.[/b] Movement uses a timed ease-in / ease-out curve. Attack, shield, healing and status effects fade in and out smoothly and last slightly longer so their results are readable. Animations do not alter dice results.

[b]Tutorial / Ability Lab.[/b] Enter directly from the opening face picker or the top bar. Select any of the 57 faces, including generated faces and penalties. Every test starts in a prepared arena with injured allies, an adjacent boss and compatible support dice. Force the next Numeric result to 0 or 1, trigger boss hits, advance a round, reroll the chosen face while preserving statuses, reset, and copy a reproducible test log. Normal loadouts are preserved.

[b]Completed face choices.[/b] Bone Mutation and Blessing of Recovery now let you choose the exact Blank slot. Corruption Conversion now asks which installed face to use, including correct when-rolled reaction handling. Passing Grace no longer destroys itself when the recipient has no Blank to receive it.

[b]Line of sight repaired.[/b] Shots and sight-based support use a straight grid ray and cannot bend around units or pass through a blocked diagonal corner.

[b]Numeric attacks strengthened in Tuned balance.[/b] A positive Numeric damage result gains +1 before face-specific bonuses. A zero remains zero; Short Shot remains capped at 1. Previously the common Numeric 1 was weaker than Basic Strike 2 and made Hooked Slash's reward difficult to use. This change applies only to Numeric Attacks, not healing or Block. Original rulebook balance keeps the old values.

[b]Balance retained where tests supported it.[/b] Tuned keeps boss HP 12, Strike 2, Brace 1, and no free Block for idle Advance. Each hero still starts with one reroll and chooses two distinct extended faces. Automated encounter results are a regression check, not a guarantee that every build has equal strength.

[b]Scope made explicit.[/b] These remain playable interpretations of draft abilities, described on each card. Cleave has no secondary enemy in this single-boss arena. Gold is recorded but has no shop in this encounter. Blank and Red Tile intentionally have no immediate effect. The Lab exposes these limits instead of treating them as broken effects.

[color=#91a0af]Previous updates · v0.3: full-pool two-face choices, causal battle logs, battlefield art and combat effects. v0.2: boss explanations, dice-roll animation, opening rerolls and selectable Tuned / Original balance.[/color]"""

const SECTIONS = [
 {"title": "Boss phases · v0.13", "body": "[b]Upgrades only at half HP[/b]\nPhase I: Cinder Brand is a five-cell cross; Ashen Chain does not Root; Furnace Roar is locked. Phase II: new Brands are 3×3, Chain adds Rooted 1 until next boss turn, and Roar unlocks. An already armed Brand keeps its marked cells.\n\n[b]Advance and Distort[/b]\nAdvance pursues highest current HP; ties random. Already adjacent to any tied highest-HP hero? Stay and gain 1 Block. Distort targets highest HP if in range, otherwise the closest in range.\n\n[b]Drive Back[/b]\nPush direction follows the hit automatically. You only choose a die if a collision causes Stunned.\n\n[b]Smoking Strike[/b]\nBoss Strike is renamed. HP damage places a fire tile under the hero. If fire is already there, consume it for 1 extra normal damage instead. Fully blocked hits do neither. Fire stays on its cell; walking onto it alone does not detonate it.\n\n[b]Read and test the phase[/b]\nHP and Block beneath the boss. A burning-crown sprite, ember rings and a brief announcement mark phase II. Rooted is visible in hover / Effects and prevents voluntary movement, including reaction steps; forced movement still works. Lab tools has Test boss phase II. Reset test returns to phase I.\n\n[b]Why[/b]\nMake the halfway change meaningful, remove player control over enemy push direction, and show what the boss is doing. Other stats are unchanged. Automated starter builds won 17/100; bonus builds 59/100, with no stalls. This is a stronger boss than v0.12. Workshop settings remain available."},
 {"title": "Playtest fixes · v0.12", "body": "[b]Strike and Numeric[/b]\nStrike now deals 1. Numeric die: 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 0 for attacks / healing / defense. Removed the old extra +1 Numeric Attack bonus. Short Shot caps at 2, including Mark.\n\n[b]Channels and growth[/b]\nStonewake breaks on any HP loss or 2 cumulative Block lost before your next own turn. Engrave grows only on HP damage, once per hero turn, into a Blank on its own die, up to 3 copies. Three copies give +1 damage; no overwriting abilities.\n\n[b]Boss phase and fire[/b]\nCinder Brand is a delayed 3×3 square. At half HP, unlock Furnace Roar: attack standing heroes within 2 for 1, then push 1; normal reactions apply. Next unresolved boss die becomes Roar; it replaces Brace on Die I for future rolls. Tuned boss HP is now 12 and its Strike deals 1, to compensate for weaker starter attacks.\n\n[b]Read the fight[/b]\nClick abilities or boss intents for a scrollable window beside the arena. Hover knights for all status values; active hero Effects are visible. HP dots return. Forge and View dice use unfolded square nets.\n\n[b]Rerolls[/b]\nThe button explains opening-window / spent / forced-result restrictions. Logs show old and new sides and explain when Blank rolls again. Lab can force Numeric 2.\n\n[b]Why these changes[/b]\nReduce runaway Channel / copy growth, make Numeric results useful, and explain choices without hiding the arena.\n\n[b]Your settings[/b]\nSaved custom values remain in force. Reset all in the balance workshop to use the new defaults. Apply restarts the fight. Soul ON/OFF remains separate.\n\n[b]Automated comparison[/b]\nStarting faces: 47 wins / 53 losses; bonus builds: 72 / 28. No stalls in either 100-seed run. These are scripted strategies, not human win rates."},
 {"title":"Balance workshop · v0.11", "body":"[b]Experiment with the actual numbers[/b]\nMenu → Game options → Balance workshop. Search an ability, boss action, Soul or passive. Edit damage, movement, ranges, Block, healing, Numeric values, reaction and Channel values, resources and body limits. Lab fixture HP / Block have their own section.\n\n[b]Blank movement[/b]\nSoul · Blank movement has both movement distance and conversions per hero turn. Defaults remain Move 2 and one use. The Soul ON/OFF switch is still separate.\n\n[b]Save, reset and share[/b]\nApply saves locally and restarts the current fight or Lab fixture. The Tuned / Original base preset is saved too. Reset a section or all values; import / export JSON to keep or share profiles. Cancel leaves the applied profile unchanged.\n\n[b]Knights and fire[/b]\nAll three heroes now wear knight armour, with distinct tabards and shields. Cinder Brand flickers while armed and flares on detonation. Ember Burst also has pixel flames. These effects do not add damage.\n\n[b]Prototype limits[/b]\nThe board, die sizes, one-die copy choices, trigger / expiry rules and one-Channel limit stay fixed. Cleave’s secondary-enemy damage is inactive in a single-boss encounter.\n\nWhy: let you test balance yourself without editing code. Default encounter values are unchanged."},
 {"title":"Pixel art & space · v0.10", "body":"[b]Pixel sprites and tiles[/b]\nReplaced the painted images with small pixel maps, limited colours and sharp nearest-neighbour scaling. Heroes have distinct full-body sprites; the boss has a larger skeletal sprite. No painted portraits remain in the game assets.\n\n[b]A much larger arena[/b]\nEach cell grows from 55 to 76 screen pixels. The board is now 684×684 instead of 495×495: about 91% more screen area. The rules still use the same 9×9 board.\n\n[b]Less clutter during combat[/b]\nOne clear turn banner. Three compact boss-intent buttons. Separate lines for each die’s name and timing. One short instruction area, reroll, and a prominent End turn button. The log remains on the right. Party cards are a compact strip below the arena.\n\n[b]Secondary tools stay out of the way[/b]\nPractice, rules, patch notes, options and rebuilding are under Menu. Lab controls are under Lab tools. View dice and Turn help stay in the toolbar. Boss intent buttons still open full descriptions.\n\nWhy: make the battlefield the focus and make the art fit a simple pixel game. Rolls stay instant; Soul settings, ability effects, dice odds and encounter balance are unchanged."},
 {"title":"Art & face picker · v0.9", "body":"[b]Instant rolls[/b]\nRemoved the rolling dice overlay and its input delay. Actual random results appear immediately on the dice and remain in the log. Attack, Block and Channel effects remain.\n\n[b]Ability names explain their timing[/b]\nNames now include tags such as (Skill - Channel), (Defense - Reaction), (Attack) and (Movement). The same labels appear in the picker, forge menus, combat dice, Lab and dice details. Abilities that grant a later reaction are not falsely marked as reactions themselves.\n\n[b]A simpler face picker[/b]\nLarger cards, hero tabs with counts, search, type and timing filters, and a fixed details panel. Click to inspect, then Add / Remove; confirm each hero when ready. The full 47-face pool remains available.\n\n[b]Painted arena and portraits[/b]\nA candlelit ruined crypt, character art and thinner grid lines replace the heavy tile boxes. Colored frames, target highlights and Channel rings remain. No combat balance or dice odds changed.\n\nWhy: faster turns, easier ability selection and a more cohesive battlefield."},
 {"title":"Clearer UI · v0.8.2", "body":"[b]Blank → Move 2 is visible during battle[/b]\nUse the ON/OFF switch directly above your action dice, or open Options in the top right. It applies immediately and to the next encounter. ON allows one rolled Blank to become Move 2 per hero turn. OFF disables this movement. Switching off and on never refreshes a spent use.\n\n[b]Clearer battle controls[/b]\nSeparate panels group the next step, boss intent, your dice and the battle log. Dice show their ability on its own line and the selected die has a stronger border. Turn help no longer overlaps the next-step explanation. The side log uses larger text.\n\n[b]Why[/b]\nThe previous switch was hidden in the forge and Lab, and the crowded UI made the next action harder to find. Combat balance and dice odds are unchanged."},
 {"title":"Test Soul · v0.8.1", "body":"[b]Enable the reward Soul before fighting[/b]\nThe forge now has a Test Soul checkbox beside Restore balanced build. ON lets each hero spend one rolled Blank as Move 2 per own turn, without first beating the boss. OFF uses the normal starting Soul.\n\nThe Lab has the same toggle, and the board shows the active hero’s remaining allowance. Switching it off and on does not refill a spent conversion. Normal and recovery turns refresh it.\n\nBuild presets save this choice. Why: make the reward Soul easy to test without a full victory first."},
 {"title":"Dice & clarity · v0.8", "body":"[b]Historical v0.8 feature; removed in v0.9[/b]\nThe current game resolves rolls instantly.\n\n[b]Real 3D dice, readable results[/b]\nHero and boss dice settle on their recorded ability faces. Numeric rolls and individual rerolls show only the affected dice. Fast rolls and Skip keep results unchanged.\n\n[b]Channel visibility[/b]\nPersistent rune rings identify Stonewake (blue), Contained Power (purple) and Last Pulse (green). Hover for its effect. Rings fade and pulse when the Channel ends.\n\n[b]More helpful controls[/b]\nReady / Spent / Reaction held / Channel held / Resolve next labels, legal-target highlights, specific error messages, friendly-fire confirmation, and a Summary / All-events log toggle.\n\n[b]Practice and presets[/b]\nEight guided lessons, a two-face Lab combination setup, ability readiness labels and Save / Load build presets. Why: make each decision visible instead of relying on the full history."},
 {"title":"Rule fixes · v0.8", "body":"[b]Pierce and Downed[/b]\nBypassed Block is no longer restored to a hero who was Downed or killed by the hit.\n\n[b]Break Rhythm[/b]\nDelays the upcoming boss activation by one slot. The original initiative order returns at the next round.\n\n[b]Short Shot cap ruling[/b]\nThe cap of 1 includes Mark Prey. A damaging hit consumes the mark, but the extra damage cannot take Short Shot above 1.\n\n[b]Channel timing ruling[/b]\nContained Power benefits from the shared roll wait for Maintain at the hero’s next turn. Releasing the Channel forfeits them.\n\n[b]Repeated Attacks[/b]\nEach repetition rechecks its target and rolls fresh Numeric damage. Hooked Slash and Engrave apply their riders to each hit.\n\nBalance constants remain unchanged; these interaction rules can still affect outcomes."},
 {"title":"Reliability · v0.7", "body":"[b]Downed heroes lose temporary effects[/b]\nReviving no longer keeps stale Numeric buffs, marks, wards, Debt or stored reaction modifiers. Physical die mutations remain.\n\n[b]Channels break on a lethal hit too[/b]\nContained Power now leaves its Red Tile and Last Pulse becomes Blank even when the triggering hit Downs or kills its hero. Damage prevention does not falsely break a Channel.\n\n[b]No silent Channel replacement[/b]\nA second Channel cannot overwrite an existing one. The game explains the current one-Channel limit; the new die can be declined.\n\n[b]Clearer documentation[/b]\nThe new short playtest guide separates current rules, ability interpretations and unfinished features. Balance values are unchanged. Why: prevent hidden state changes during ordinary play."},
 {"title":"Reward Soul · v0.6", "body":"[b]One Blank conversion per hero turn[/b]\n\nThe first boss reward Soul lets each hero spend at most ONE rolled Action Die Blank as Move 2 during their turn. The installed face stays Blank. Other Blanks may be spent without an effect.\n\nThe allowance resets at that hero’s next normal turn or full recovery turn. It is independent for each hero. Failed moves do not spend it. Rerolls and shared rolls do not refill it during the same turn.\n\n[b]Why[/b]\nKeeps the reward useful without letting multiple Blank rolls replace dedicated movement faces. The starting Soul still gives no Blank movement.\n\nA separate Word comparison documents changes from Master Rules v10 and Action Faces, including unresolved-design interpretations and omitted systems."},
 {"title":"Overview", "body":"[b]v0.5 · More choices, clearer turns[/b]\n\n• Two Blanks minimum per die, with fuller default builds.\n• Ashstep and Oathbound Exchange join the full starter-choice pool.\n• View dice shows every installed side, its die, current result and encounter changes.\n• Explain this turn gives steps, timing and the next action.\n• The boss pulls, steals Block and marks delayed explosions.\n\n[b]Why[/b]\nFewer dead rolls, more useful movement and fewer hidden rules. Use the topic buttons to jump directly to details."},
 {"title":"Dice & turn flow", "body":"[b]Two Blanks instead of three.[/b]\nEach die may now hold four abilities: up to 12 total. Default builds add a fourth Strike, a second Step and a second Guard. Ownership and the three-per-category caps still apply.\n\n[b]Why[/b]\nEmpty rolls dominated play. Extra useful faces create more decisions; one saved starting reroll remains. This construction change applies in both encounter modes.\n\n[b]Turn explanations[/b]\nThe chronicle explains turn starts; Explain this turn covers rerolls, available dice, targets, reactions, Block expiry and shared round rolls. View dice distinguishes installed faces from already-recorded results."},
 {"title":"New movement", "body":"[b]Ashstep[/b]\nMove up to 2 orthogonal spaces, turning allowed, then gain 1 Block. Occupied cells block the path.\n\n[b]Oathbound Exchange[/b]\nSwap with a standing ally within 3 and clear sight. Both heroes gain 1 Block. Cannot target the boss, a dead ally or a Downed ally.\n\n[b]Why[/b]\nAshstep supports safe repositioning. Exchange rescues an ally or changes the front line. Both help escape Cinder Brand. Choose them from the 47-face extended pool or try them in the Lab."},
 {"title":"Boss changes", "body":"[b]Ashen Chain[/b]\nPull the nearest hero within 3 one legal cell closer and strip 1 Block. No HP damage.\n\n[b]Cinder Brand[/b]\nMark a red cross under a hero within 3. At the next boss turn start, heroes still on it take 1 normal damage. Move away to evade. Brands cannot stack.\n\n[b]Grave Tithe[/b]\nSteal 1 Block from each standing hero within 2, gaining at most 2 Block.\n\n[b]Why[/b]\nThe boss now pressures positioning and defense instead of repeating attacks. Tuned HP is 16 to account for fuller hero dice. Original encounter mode retains the previous boss dice and 18 HP."},
 {"title":"Fixes & previous", "body":"[b]Navigation[/b]\nPatch notes have topic buttons, Previous / Next and a page counter. Short pages replace one long scroll. Escape closes reference windows.\n\n[b]Live dice inspection[/b]\nGold marks mutations and displays the original face. Blue marks rolled sides. Details explain generated Bone / Recovery, locked Red Tiles, reaction / Channel holds and results recorded before a mutation.\n\n[b]Earlier updates[/b]\nv0.4: Ability Lab, side chronicle, turn banner, eased animations, explicit mutation / conversion choices and Numeric attack tuning.\nv0.3: two-face gifts, causal combat logs and battlefield art.\nv0.2: boss explanations and starting rerolls.\n\n[b]Scope[/b]\nA local single-boss prototype. Gold has no shop; Cleave has no secondary enemy. All extended effects print their playable interpretations."}
]
